  "name": "stitch::extract-design-md",
  "description": "Extract a comprehensive design system (DESIGN.md) directly from frontend source code — React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, plain HTML/CSS, or any web framework. Analyzes component files, stylesheets, Tailwind configs, theme definitions, and design tokens to produce a rich, Stitch-compatible design system document. Use this skill whenever the user wants to reverse-engineer a design system from an existing codebase, audit the visual language of a project, extract design tokens from source files, or understand the styling patterns in a frontend repo — even if they just say \"what does this app look like?\" or \"pull out the design from this code.\" Also use this skill when the user only has a live website URL — a client site, a reference site, or a product whose code isn't available — and wants its design system extracted as a DESIGN.md, even if they just give the URL and say \"pull the design from this site.\"",
